WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
(audience clapping)
(upbeat trumpet music)

00:00:10.914 --> 00:00:13.914
(audience cheering)

00:00:25.665 --> 00:00:26.665
- Thank you.

00:00:27.772 --> 00:00:29.195
- [Audience Member] We love you, Angela!

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.278
- I love you!

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.930
Regina, my dear, dear Regina.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:37.763
My sister,

00:00:37.763 --> 00:00:40.030
thank you for being here tonight

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:46.010
as a source of support
and encouragement and joy.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.630
Working alongside you has been one

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.180
of the highlights of my career.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:56.180
You are for me, and for so
many, a bright, bright light.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.545
Thank you.

00:00:59.545 --> 00:01:02.545
(audience clapping)

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:09.510
It is because of the love
and support of my friends

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:13.143
and my family that I
stand here this evening.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:19.130
I offer a lifetime and beyond of gratitude

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:24.060
to my sister, Danette,
my husband, Courtney,

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:28.863
and our beautiful children,
Bronwyn and Slater.

00:01:30.121 --> 00:01:32.940
(audience clapping)

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.250
Whom I'm blessed to have
with me this evening.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.273
Rest on your feet.

00:01:37.714 --> 00:01:39.093
Look at 'em.

00:01:39.093 --> 00:01:42.093
(audience clapping)

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:51.230
They have each in their own
way made space in our lives

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:56.340
to allow me the freedom
to be a sister, a mother,

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:59.613
a wife, and an actor.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:02.733
I love you wholly and deeply.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:08.460
To the women who shower
me with heavenly love,

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.640
my mother Betty and my aunt Golden,

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.100
both who loved and nurtured me

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.580
in spite of their concerns that I chose

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:21.034
to use my Yale degrees to pursue acting.

00:02:21.034 --> 00:02:22.830
(audience laughing)

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:24.360
I say thank you.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:29.297
Thank you for the gift of
allowing me to chase my dreams.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.873
Thank you to my amazing team,

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:39.740
Darrell, Leslie, Steven,
Jeffrey, Bill, Anita,

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:44.370
Gilda, DeAndre, Jennifer, Randy,

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:48.330
as well as Bassett Vance
Productions, Lynette,

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.253
Lonnie, Eric, and Chelsea.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.440
I sincerely appreciate
all that you do with me

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.813
and for me each day.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:01.950
Thank you to every director,

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.590
casting director, producer, studio exec,

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:07.320
costume designer, hair and makeup team,

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.030
production design team,

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:13.140
as well as fellow cast members and crew

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:16.950
whom I've had the
pleasure to work alongside

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:18.663
while making magic.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:20.523
Thank you.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.680
Thank you to the Academy

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:29.840
and the Board of Governors
for this, this award.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:35.613
I have considered acting my
calling and not just my career.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:39.610
I do this work because
I find it meaningful

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:43.740
and I hope in some way
that it makes a difference

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.840
and has an impact.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.730
To be recognized in this
way for what I love doing

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:55.730
is truly wonderful, and
I am beyond grateful.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.507
You know, Lena Horne once said,

00:03:58.507 --> 00:04:00.870
"It's so nice to get flowers

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:03.930
while you can yet still
smell the fragrance,"

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.821
and indeed it is.

00:04:06.821 --> 00:04:09.720
(audience laughing)

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:10.553
You know,

00:04:10.553 --> 00:04:13.210
I have had to let it sink in that

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:19.220
I am the second Black actress
to receive an honorary Oscar,

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:24.090
the first being my dear friend and mentor,

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:27.484
the late Cicely Tyson in 2018.

00:04:27.484 --> 00:04:30.484
(audience clapping)

00:04:33.137 --> 00:04:35.070
Having a chance to work with

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:39.510
and learn from Ms. Tyson is
one of the most memorable

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:44.430
and treasured experiences
of my career and life,

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:49.320
and I hope that she is
smiling from the heavens

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:54.320
that I'm able to join her in
this circle of recognition

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:58.860
Knowing that she was so impactful to me

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:02.313
as an actress and as a woman.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:07.983
I thought long and hard about
what I'd say this evening.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:13.473
This for me is not just another award,

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:16.770
it's a testament to my legacy.

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:21.650
This trophy represents my contributions

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:23.313
to this medium of film,

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:27.960
all that I've given of my mind, body,

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:32.913
and spirit as an actress
who is a Black woman.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.250
So,

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:38.190
do I go the route of saying
a few words of gratitude for

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.290
what this moment means to me

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:44.790
or do I give voice to what I hope

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:47.910
this moment should mean for generations

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.743
of Black actresses to come?

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:52.260
As I look to the future,

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:55.230
I think that it would be of service

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:59.190
to face that which we all must contend

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:01.740
as we look toward tomorrow and beyond.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:06.740
So, if you will open
your hearts and minds,

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.543
I'll just share my personal reflection.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:16.040
And we're days away from
Martin Luther King Jr. holiday.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:19.770
And something he once
said touched my spirit

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:22.170
in thinking about what I
would say this evening.

00:06:23.497 --> 00:06:28.350
"We are not makers of history.

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:32.367
We are made by history."

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:37.620
To put what this moment means to me

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.090
in historical context,

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:43.587
my mind traveled back
to February 29th, 1940,

00:06:43.587 --> 00:06:46.353
the 12th Annual Academy Award,

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:49.530
the ceremony when actor, singer,

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:52.230
songwriting Hadie McDaniel became

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:56.927
the first Black person
to ever win an Oscar.

00:06:56.927 --> 00:06:59.927
(audience clapping)

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:06.980
Before she took the stage, the
actress, Fay Bainter, said,

00:07:07.237 --> 00:07:10.111
"It is more than a plaque of gold."

00:07:10.111 --> 00:07:10.944
- [Audience Member] Yes!

00:07:10.944 --> 00:07:13.800
- "It opens the doors of this room.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:16.050
It moves back the walls

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:20.670
and enables us to embrace
the whole of America,

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:25.380
an America that almost is
alone in the world today.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:28.290
It recognizes and pays tribute

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:31.500
to those who have given their best,

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:35.487
regardless of creed, race, or color."

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:40.360
It was at this point that Ms. McDaniel

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:46.230
walked from the back of that
Coconut Grove restaurant,

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:49.357
passed the table where her fellow

00:07:49.357 --> 00:07:51.150
"Gone with the Wind" castmates

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:53.820
and studio executives were seated,

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:57.960
that she historically tore down a barrier,

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:00.510
making it possible for Black actresses

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:04.320
to be seen and recognized
at the highest levels in our

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:08.155
industry for their contribution on film.

00:08:08.155 --> 00:08:11.155
(audience clapping)

00:08:16.159 --> 00:08:18.180
And it would be another 50 years

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:21.780
before another Black
woman would win an Oscar,

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:23.700
that extraordinary woman being

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:26.040
my dear sister friend, Whoopi,

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:28.380
and still more than a decade

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:32.490
before the next historical
milestone with Halle's win

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:34.080
as best actress,

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:39.080
which for more than two
decades remains the only.

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:45.420
We have Jennifer,
Monique, Octavia, Lupita,

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:49.353
Viola, Regina, and Ariana,

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:55.550
10 actresses who are makers
of history in our industry.

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:58.260
I call their names to
acknowledge every one

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:01.980
of them this evening for
being beacons of possibility

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:04.170
and hope for little Black

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:08.190
and Brown girls who aspire to one day

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:11.703
pursue the dream of becoming an actor.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:14.370
When acting took hold of my heart,

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:19.370
there was not a clear path to
what success could look like

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.020
because there were so few,

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:25.020
so few Black actresses in prominent roles,

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:26.580
in television or film.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:30.480
For me, those trailblazing actors,

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:32.310
like Ruby Dee, Diahann Carroll,

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:34.920
Cicely Tyson, and Rosalind Cash,

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:38.100
they were my North Star
and my guiding light,

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:42.190
proof that while the road may

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:46.860
not be without curves and bumps,

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:49.800
there was a way to fulfill what I

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:52.893
believed deep in my soul was my destiny.

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:59.060
So it was that standing on their strong,

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:03.120
spiritually fortified shoulders

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:06.300
that I often was sustained,

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:10.470
and I thank them for every sacrifice,

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:15.270
every doubt, every
disappointment, every rejection,

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:19.710
every triumph that I know
they experienced along the way

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:22.620
because had it not been
for their resilience,

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:26.490
continuing to fight through
their fears and the uncertainty

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:31.200
and their willingness as
they fought for every role,

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:34.290
I would not have had a representation of

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:37.113
what was possible for me.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:43.490
But this honor isn't just for or about me.

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:48.720
What I hope this moment means is

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:52.170
that we are taking the necessary
steps toward a future in

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:57.170
which it is the norm, not the exception,

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:02.720
to see and embrace one
another's full humanity,

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:07.770
stories, and perspectives.

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.600
This must be our goal

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:14.600
and to always remember that
there is room for us all.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:19.263
When we stand together, we win together.

00:11:21.534 --> 00:11:24.534
(audience clapping)

00:11:30.864 --> 00:11:33.447
To my fellow Black actresses...

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:35.933
- Yes!
- Yes!

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:42.450
- Fill your hearts with
courage and strength.

00:11:42.450 --> 00:11:45.990
Because regardless of what
you may think or see or feel,

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:48.810
your contributions do matter.

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:53.010
Take comfort knowing
that your performances

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:57.030
have given hope, offered
a different perspective,

00:11:57.030 --> 00:12:01.710
and for others, just pure
joy in a time of need.

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:05.850
Never allow fear, frustration,

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:09.780
or disappointment to get
in the way of the blessings

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:14.780
that are divinely and deservedly yours.

00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:20.090
Remember who you are and who our ancestors

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:23.493
intended you to be, us to be.

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:27.120
I proudly share this honor with women

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:31.890
who stand up when they
are told to stand back,

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:34.860
who speak up when they are silenced,

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:39.630
who remain determined when they
are told they are defeated.

00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:42.660
These women represent those
that I've had the honor

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:47.660
to portray as well as the
everyday woman who surround us

00:12:47.940 --> 00:12:51.603
and inspire us to keep striving.

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:55.833
And to everyone in this room,

00:12:56.910 --> 00:13:00.990
I say when it comes to what
we do, the decisions we make,

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:03.120
how we embrace one another,

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:06.390
how we should support
and lift up one another,

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:10.710
always remember that the
stakes are extremely high

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:14.220
because history depends on us.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:15.053
Why?

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:18.780
Because we are the lens

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:23.283
through which future
generations will see themselves.

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:29.420
And my prayer is that we leave
this industry more enriched,

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:34.320
forward thinking, and
inclusive than we found it,

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:39.320
a future where there won't
be a first or an only,

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:43.860
or suspense around whether
history will be made

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:46.320
with a nomination or a win.

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:49.170
I have faith that one day, someday,

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:51.600
the celebration and recognition

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:56.550
will be solely on the
performance and the performer.

00:13:56.550 --> 00:13:58.353
Because at the end of the day,

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:04.350
we all just want to have the opportunity

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:07.743
to do great, meaningful work.

00:14:08.874 --> 00:14:11.874
(audience clapping)

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:19.657
Maya Angelou said very wisely,

00:14:19.657 --> 00:14:21.180
"People will forget.

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:23.010
They will forget what you said.

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:24.150
People will forget.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:25.770
They will forget what you did.

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:30.770
But people will never forget
the way you made them feel."

00:14:31.216 --> 00:14:32.760
(audience clapping)

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.610
To all who have been
on this journey with me

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:37.110
and supported the films in which

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:39.360
I've had the privilege to play,

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:42.570
it is my profound honor

00:14:42.570 --> 00:14:47.010
to have been able to make you
see and feel through my work.

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:51.870
Thank you for sharing this moment with me.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:56.870
And still, I say, the best is yet to come.

00:14:57.865 --> 00:14:59.422
(audience cheering)

00:14:59.422 --> 00:15:02.672
(bright trumpet music)

